---
description: Defines standards for Vue 3 component design, including Composition API usage, props/emits typing, naming conventions, and style scoping.
globs: "**/*.vue"
---
- All components must use Vue 3 Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">`.
- Component file names must use PascalCase (e.g., UserProfile.vue, TodoList.vue).
- Props must be defined using `defineProps<T>()` with a TypeScript interface.
- Use `withDefaults(defineProps<T>(), { ... })` when default values are needed.
- Emits must be explicitly typed using `defineEmits<{ (e: 'eventName', payload: Type): void }>()`.
- Use `<style scoped>` to prevent CSS leakage between components.
- Components should follow the single responsibility principle — one component, one purpose.
- Extract reusable logic into composables (src/composables/) rather than duplicating code across components.
- Template expressions should be simple. Move complex logic into computed properties or methods.
- Avoid using `v-html` unless absolutely necessary (XSS risk). Sanitize content if used.
- Use `v-for` with `:key` always bound to a unique identifier, never an index (unless the list is static).
- Reusable UI components go in src/components/. Page-level components (route targets) go in src/views/.
